// healthz-and-restarts.kql — best-effort proxy for "/healthz failures" (gap
// 4.6). HONEST LIMITATION: the app has no per-request access log today (no
// status-code line is emitted for any route, healthz included — grep
// internal/cloudserver/api/*.go, there is no s.log call in the request path
// other than a handful of error-branch Warns/Errors unrelated to healthz). A
// direct "/healthz returned 5xx" alert therefore cannot be built from
// Log Analytics as instrumented today; adding a structured per-request log
// line (status, route, latency) is the owed follow-up that would make a real
// version of this alert possible.
//
// Until then, this is the closest real signal: repeated container EXITS /
// restarts on sbci-api, which is what a sustained /healthz failure produces
// (ACA restarts a container whose configured liveness/startup probe — which
// IS /healthz per the Container Apps default — keeps failing).
ContainerAppSystemLogs_CL
| where TimeGenerated > ago(15m)
| where ContainerAppName_s == "sbci-api"
| where Log_s has_any ("ProcessExited", "Started", "Pulling")
| summarize restarts = countif(Log_s has "ProcessExited") by bin(TimeGenerated, 5m), RevisionName_s
| where restarts >= 2
| order by TimeGenerated desc
